The independent behavior check found the generated solution correct against the mathematical contract on all 22,748 valid cases. It also found a real reference-solution limitation: the trusted canonical uses floating-point division, so it returns `True` for `9007199254740993/2 × 1/1` and raises `OverflowError` on a 401-digit numerator, while the generated modulo implementation returns the mathematically intended `False`. I’ll keep that discrepancy explicit rather than treating the canonical as a flawless oracle.
