@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if [[ $# -lt 2 ]]; then
+  echo "usage: run_logged.sh LOG COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 64
+fi
+
+log_path=$1
+shift
+
+{
+  printf 'cwd: %q\n' "$PWD"
+  printf 'command:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+} >"$log_path"
+
+set +e
+"$@" > >(tee -a "$log_path") 2> >(tee -a "$log_path" >&2)
+command_status=$?
+set -e
+
+printf 'exit_status: %d\n' "$command_status" | tee -a "$log_path"
+exit "$command_status"

codex
The static review is now focused on the three proof-local simplifications. They are result-bearing, so I tested them against the base semantics rather than accepting their names: representative positive, zero, and negative ground instances close, and K’s installed builtin contract says `Int2String` emits signed decimal digits while `String2Int` parses that syntax. However, bridge-free universal claims remain stuck because the symbolic backend treats those string hooks opaquely. That is a trust/evidence limitation I will account for explicitly; it is not a witnessed false equation.
